"""Human-readable experiment tables, computed from the logged exact radii."""
import collections,json
from decimal import Decimal as D
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];S=json.loads((ROOT/'summary.json').read_text())
gate=lambda r:max(D('1e-10'),D(r)*D('1e-8'))
lines=['# Experiment evidence','','These are descriptive results from one heavily loaded Apple M2 machine. No population success probability or statistical speedup is inferred. All counts use common original starts in the held-out comparison; continuation uses a separate stronger frozen input set.','','## Held-out paired comparison','','Both arms received 45-second block budgets. “Winner” requires a radius difference beyond the practical gate. The CPU-matched sensitivity analysis retains only complete trial endpoints within the smaller observed CPU budget; it was added after timing imbalance was observed.','','| Seed | N | Original best r | Targeted best r | Wall-budget winner | Common CPU s | CPU-matched winner |','|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---|']
for m in S['matched']:lines.append(f"|{m['replicate']}|{m['n']}|{m['arms']['original']['best_radius']}|{m['arms']['targeted']['best_radius']}|{m['winner']}|{m['posthoc_common_cpu_seconds']:.2f}|{m['cpu_matched_winner']}|")
lines+=['','Wall-budget outcomes: '+str(dict(collections.Counter(m['winner'] for m in S['matched'])))+'. CPU-matched outcomes: '+str(dict(collections.Counter(m['cpu_matched_winner'] for m in S['matched'])))+'.','',
        '## Stronger-start continuation','','Two methods × two seeds at N=500/800; two additional seeds per method at N=700, added after its held-out discovery. Each block starts from the same frozen best witness for that N. This is a deliberately selected promising subset, not a random sample of all N.','','| Seed | N | Method | Stronger starting r | Best final r | Additional gain | Clears gate? | CPU s | Wall s |','|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|']
for b in S['blocks']:
 if b['phase'].startswith('continuation-'):
  delta=D(b['best_radius'])-D(b['start_radius']);lines.append(f"|{b['replicate']}|{b['n']}|{b['arm']}|{b['start_radius']}|{b['best_radius']}|{delta:+.3E}|{'yes' if delta>gate(b['start_radius']) else 'no'}|{b['cpu_seconds']:.2f}|{b['wall_seconds']:.2f}|")
lines+=['','## Plain longer polishing and A/A repeat','','The first polish-only control uses the unchanged pre-session input, no perturbation and up to 90 seconds / 3,000 LP steps. The final strong-polish diagnostic uses the newest post-continuation witness and up to 120 seconds. Stationarity may stop either early. A/A repeats original N=500 seed 0 at a later wall-clock time. These diagnostic controls were added during the session and are not randomized treatment estimates.','','| Phase | N | Best r | Gain from its input | CPU s | Wall s |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for b in S['blocks']:
 if b['phase'] in ['long-polish','strong-polish','aa-original-repeat'] or (b['phase']=='exploration-original' and b['n']==500):
  lines.append(f"|{b['phase']}|{b['n']}|{b['best_radius']}|{D(b['best_radius'])-D(b['start_radius']):+.3E}|{b['cpu_seconds']:.2f}|{b['wall_seconds']:.2f}|")
lines+=['','## Trial accounting','','“Above start” includes repeated recovery, not independent discoveries. “Recovered” includes ties within the gate, excludes initial unperturbed polish, and compares moves of different disruption sizes. It is a repair diagnostic, not a fair hardness ranking of neighborhoods.','','| Stage | Method | Trials | Above input gate | Recovered / perturbed | LP steps | LP failure/limit trials | CPU s | Wall s |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for m in S['mode_stats']:lines.append(f"|{m['stage']}|{m['arm']}|{m['trials']}|{m['above_block_start_trials']}|{m['recovered_start_within_gate']}/{m['nonpolish_trials']}|{m['lp_steps']}|{m['lp_failure_trials']}|{m['cpu_seconds']:.2f}|{m['wall_seconds']:.2f}|")
lines+=['',f"Total: {S['trials']} saved trial witnesses; {S['completed_blocks']} completed blocks; {S['worker_wall_seconds']:.2f} worker wall seconds; {S['worker_cpu_seconds']:.2f} worker CPU seconds; {S['peak_worker_rss_bytes']/1024**2:.1f} MiB peak worker RSS.",'',
        '## Interpretation limits','','- Repeated seeds are a small formative check; no statistical confidence interval is warranted.','- A local stationary solution is not a global optimum. A null in this budget does not establish that the mathematical instance is saturated.','- Wall time includes certificate construction and checking. CPU timing counts this worker, not unrelated system processes or agent inference.','- Algorithms were not compared against a full PBTS or other state-of-the-art implementation. These are the existing pilot solver and a session-designed variant.','- The trial log key `gain_vs_session_start` means gain from that block’s chosen input; continuation blocks use the stronger input. Global session gains in RESULTS.md and summary.json are independently recomputed from the original frozen witness.','- Source code hashes were captured per block. The paired-arm search code froze at af6be839e2c83fa04353dcf4969af7a54858409d. Later additions were separately logged polishing controls, analysis, exact accounting, visualization and scheduling; the two compared strategies stayed unchanged.','']
(ROOT/'EXPERIMENTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
